Changes for Orchestra/Maestro, 2026:
- A: ported computation, strict validation, canonical capability discovery,
  lazy selected handlers and a shared standalone MCP transport.
- B: ported scoped repository/compiler/parser acquisition, physical path
  fencing, bounded coverage and explicitly authorized materialization.
- C: adapted TechLead doctrine into demand-loaded Maestro playbooks and
  Composer guidance; native authority remains with the Orchestra host.
- D: ported project-isolated bounded governance state, provenance-aware
  evidence, replay scheduling and selective recovery without Git reset/clean.
- E: added native Core/OpenCode adapters for progressive discovery,
  exact schema execution and host-owned identity/permissions.
- F: adapted recognized command/output checks at native tool boundaries;
  remaining host-binding gaps are not claims of delivered enforcement.
- Integration: connected actual owner descriptors, registered governance,
  froze authorization resources and added workspace runtime dependencies.

